# Requirements: TBD change title

Grammar: one level-two heading per requirement that starts with its
identifier, a Change line (add, modify or remove), a statement with an
uppercase normative keyword, then one or more level-three scenarios with
Given/When/Then steps. A removed requirement needs a Reason line instead of
scenarios.

## REQ-001 TBD requirement title

Change: add
The TBD component MUST TBD observable obligation.

### Scenario: TBD ordinary case

- Given TBD concrete precondition with real values
- When TBD single action
- Then TBD observable outcome
- And TBD further observable outcome

### Scenario: TBD boundary case

- Given TBD precondition at the limit (empty, maximum, exactly at threshold)
- When TBD single action
- Then TBD observable outcome

### Scenario: TBD failure case

- Given TBD precondition that makes the action invalid or unauthorized
- When TBD single action
- Then TBD error outcome with a stable error identifier
- But TBD state that must not change

## REQ-002 TBD modified requirement title

Change: modify
Previously: TBD the old statement from the living spec.
The TBD component SHOULD TBD new obligation, except when TBD documented case.

### Scenario: TBD new behavior

- Given TBD precondition
- When TBD single action
- Then TBD observable outcome

